-- title:
--   Localisation of a lattice intersection at a finite place
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring that is also a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra, and let $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $D$ such that each is finitely generated and each spans $D$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. $\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Lambda_i)=\top$ for $i=1,2$ (so in particular $D$ is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$ and both $\Lambda_i$ are full lattices). Let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, a finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$, with adic completion $\mathbb{Q}_v$ and valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$ inside it. For a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda \subseteq D$, [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\, v$ denotes the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by all elementary tensors $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c \in \mathcal{O}_v$. The assertion is the equality of additive subgroups of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$
--   $$\text{localBox}(\Lambda_1 \sqcap \Lambda_2, v) \;=\; \text{localBox}(\Lambda_1, v) \sqcap \text{localBox}(\Lambda_2, v),$$
--   where $\Lambda_1 \sqcap \Lambda_2$ is the intersection of the two $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules and the right-hand intersection is taken in the lattice of additive subgroups.
--
--   This is the standard compatibility of localisation of lattices with finite intersections: completing at a finite place commutes with intersecting two full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattices in a finite-dimensional $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra. It is used in the construction and recognition of Eichler orders as intersections of two maximal orders, where the local picture of the intersection at each finite place must be read off from the local pictures of the two factors.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_localBox_inf.lean

